{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Trust, etc.</b> Therefore fathers say to sons: Trust in the name." "The bet of 'ביה' serves as a particle, per standard rule." "<b>Rock.</b> A stronghold forever. For there are those in the books who combine alef-bet with the Name, which is half the Name in number of letters, and in the Book of Tehillot I shall explain this on the verse 'Extol him who rides on the clouds' (Psalms 68:5)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {2 "'Book of Tehillot' likely refers to Ibn Ezra's commentary on Psalms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:11.053172579Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}